1
00:05:56,666 --> 00:06:02,666
World War Two was just ending. World War Murphy is about to begin.

2
00:11:53,333 --> 00:11:59,333
Murphy's War is a drama, war film directed by Peter Yates.

3
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Murphy is the sole survivor of his crew, that has been massacred by a
German U-Boat in the closing days of World War II.

4
00:23:46,666 --> 00:23:52,666
He is rescued, and ends up at a forgotten mission station near the
mouth of the Orinoco, and begins to plot his vengeance.

5
00:29:43,333 --> 00:29:49,333
He wishes to sink the U-Boat by means of any method imaginable to him, and sets about to make the
courageous attempt, assisted by Louis, the administrator of the local oil company.

6
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:46,000
Murphy, played by Peter O'Toole.

7
00:41:36,666 --> 00:41:42,666
Hayden, played by Siân Phillips.

8
00:47:33,333 --> 00:47:39,333
Brezan, played by Philippe Noiret.

9
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:36,000
Lauchs, played by Horst Janson.

10
00:59:26,666 --> 00:59:32,666
Ellis, played by John Hallam.

11
01:05:23,333 --> 01:05:29,333
Voght, played by Ingo Mogendorf.

12
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:26,000
Murphy's War is an Eastmancolor 1971 Panavision war film
starring Peter O'Toole and Siân Phillips.

13
01:17:16,666 --> 01:17:22,666
It was directed by Peter Yates, based on the 1969 novel by Max Catto.

14
01:23:13,333 --> 01:23:19,333
The film's cinematographer was Douglas Slocombe.

15
01:29:10,000 --> 01:29:16,000
The film is set in Venezuela during World War II and focuses on a stubborn survivor of a sunken merchant ship who is consumed in his
quest for revenge and retribution against the Nazi German submarine that sank his ship and slaughtered the survivors.

16
01:35:06,666 --> 01:35:12,666
The film explores themes of submarine, world war
ii, revenge, crane, sole survivor.

17
01:41:03,333 --> 01:41:09,333
The tone is emotional.
